# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin panel password (/admin)
#
# One variable. It is the password you type, and it also signs the session
# cookie — changing it signs out every device. It opens /dashboard as you too,
# which is how you get the list of every client. Use something long: beside the
# database credentials, it is the only thing standing in front of your data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enquiry storage (MongoDB Atlas) — where every enquiry is kept
#
# This is the only delivery path. There is no email service: enquiries are
# written here, and you read them at /admin. Without it the form still works,
# but it can only offer the visitor a pre-filled email instead.
#
# Create a free M0 cluster at https://www.mongodb.com/atlas, add a database
# user, allow access from anywhere (0.0.0.0/0) under Network Access — Vercel
# Functions have no fixed IP address — then copy the connection string from
# Connect -> Drivers and put your database name on the end:
#   mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/sawyer
#
# Set it in Vercel -> your project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, then
# redeploy. The README has a step-by-step walkthrough and the errors to expect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MONGODB_URI=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client dashboards (/dashboard)
#
# Nothing extra to set: clients sign in with the code they are given when they
# send an enquiry, and that code opens their own dashboard only. The admin
# password above also opens /dashboard as the admin, which is how you get the
# list of every client. Without MONGODB_URI the client side of the dashboard is
# simply switched off and the sign-in page says so.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical site URL (optional)
#
# Used for canonical tags, Open Graph, the sitemap and the JSON-LD. On Vercel
# this is worked out for you from the project's production domain, so leave it
# empty unless you want to force a particular one — then set it to your domain
# including the scheme, e.g. https://yourdomain.com. It is baked in at build
# time, so a change needs a redeploy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare R2 Media Storage (/dashboard)
#
# Enables direct S3-compatible asset uploads for client dashboards (logos,
# graphics, style guides, and photos) with zero egress fees.
# If these are not set, media uploads fall back safely to database storage.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_BUCKET=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_PUBLIC_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PayPal Invoicing & Payments (/invoice/[id])
#
# Generates private, secure single-page invoices that clients can pay via
# PayPal, debit/credit cards, and Pay in 4.
#
# Obtain your Client ID and Secret at https://developer.paypal.com/dashboard:
# 1. Apps & Credentials -> Create App (or use default Live/Sandbox app)
# 2. Copy Client ID and Secret
# 3. Add to Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables:
#    - PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID: Your PayPal Client ID
#    - PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET: Your PayPal Client Secret (never exposed to browser)
#    - PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT: "live" (or "sandbox" for testing)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT=live
